{"from": "text:tacitus-annals-15-44", "type": "attests", "to": "person:jesus-of-nazareth", "grade": "A", "note": "Tacitus, Annals 15.44: 'Christus, from whom the name had its origin, suffered the extreme penalty during the reign of Tiberius at the hands of one of our procurators, Pontius Pilatus' - the Roman historian names the movement's founder as Christus (the name by which the person node is called) and places his execution under Pilate in Tiberius's reign."}
